00:55:29.110 --> 00:55:29.943
All right.

00:55:29.943 --> 00:55:33.008
So first of all, there was no--

00:55:33.008 --> 00:55:33.841
Sponsor.

00:55:33.841 --> 00:55:35.610
Because there was no sponsor language

00:55:35.610 --> 00:55:36.443
at the end,

00:55:36.443 --> 00:55:37.960
because, here's the thing.

00:55:37.960 --> 00:55:40.184
We were at a desperate point,

00:55:40.184 --> 00:55:43.200
we were trying to scrap together a living,

00:55:43.200 --> 00:55:45.330
we had started Good Mythical Morning,

00:55:45.330 --> 00:55:47.970
but we weren't making
money off of it really.

00:55:47.970 --> 00:55:52.300
So it was, I'm just saying,
we were a bit desperate

00:55:52.300 --> 00:55:54.537
to feed our families,
don't hold this against us,

00:55:54.537 --> 00:55:58.310
but you know, the final
product that we created

00:55:58.310 --> 00:55:59.380
was not icky,

00:55:59.380 --> 00:56:01.910
it actually had a good feeling.

00:56:01.910 --> 00:56:03.300
But which one is worse?

00:56:03.300 --> 00:56:04.133
It felt good, right?

00:56:04.133 --> 00:56:05.803
From a moral perspective.

00:56:06.680 --> 00:56:08.310
Let's just really explore this.

00:56:08.310 --> 00:56:13.310
Which one is worse, one
that most intelligent people

00:56:13.810 --> 00:56:16.550
believe was real, but was fake,

00:56:16.550 --> 00:56:19.184
or ones that the person
who makes the video

00:56:19.184 --> 00:56:21.480
has already dealt with
the fact that they make

00:56:21.480 --> 00:56:23.601
prank videos, fake prank videos,

00:56:23.601 --> 00:56:25.810
and they constantly get accused of it,

00:56:25.810 --> 00:56:27.420
but they just keep making the videos,

00:56:27.420 --> 00:56:30.757
and there's a bit of a
knowingness between them

00:56:30.757 --> 00:56:32.560
and the audience that this is all fake,

00:56:32.560 --> 00:56:34.410
but you're still watching it.

00:56:34.410 --> 00:56:36.010
Which one is more morally wrong?

00:56:37.450 --> 00:56:39.150
I know which one is a worse video.

00:56:40.424 --> 00:56:41.980
The whole knowingness thing,

00:56:41.980 --> 00:56:44.480
I just don't think that's
legitimate across the board.

00:56:44.480 --> 00:56:46.042
I agree, I was playing devil's advocate.

00:56:46.042 --> 00:56:50.289
So I don't think this is a fair question.

00:56:50.289 --> 00:56:52.370
I mean, I never talked to Roman Atwood

00:56:52.370 --> 00:56:54.485
about his switch, you know?

00:56:54.485 --> 00:56:57.970
He really made a name for
himself with his prank videos,

00:56:57.970 --> 00:57:01.563
pranking his own family and
I think other people too,

00:57:02.850 --> 00:57:05.510
but then he totally switched
it to just like a family

00:57:05.510 --> 00:57:07.553
vlogger, promoting positivity.

00:57:08.501 --> 00:57:10.790
And then he totally stopped making videos.

00:57:10.790 --> 00:57:12.700
I don't know why he made, he did?

00:57:12.700 --> 00:57:14.120
He's not making videos at all?

00:57:14.120 --> 00:57:15.950
He made a couple in the past year.

00:57:15.950 --> 00:57:19.220
Talk about running the YouTube gauntlet.

00:57:19.220 --> 00:57:22.240
Starting out with prank
videos and then trying

00:57:22.240 --> 00:57:23.704
to figure out what makes people angry

00:57:23.704 --> 00:57:25.787
when they watch it.

00:57:25.787 --> 00:57:28.700
There's people who are just mean-spirited,

00:57:28.700 --> 00:57:30.800
taking advantage of people.

00:57:30.800 --> 00:57:33.620
There was lots of stuff
done in poor taste,

00:57:33.620 --> 00:57:34.920
and I'm not talking about Roman Atwood,

00:57:34.920 --> 00:57:37.020
I'm just talking about prank videos.

00:57:37.020 --> 00:57:39.165
But he was, a guy like him in that world,

00:57:39.165 --> 00:57:41.488
we sidestepped that world,
we just dabbled in this

00:57:41.488 --> 00:57:43.294
one video, really.

00:57:43.294 --> 00:57:48.294
Once we had a sizeable
audience, but then he jumps over

00:57:49.840 --> 00:57:54.215
to family vlogging which
is another death gauntlet

00:57:54.215 --> 00:57:57.620
of personal health.

00:57:57.620 --> 00:57:59.130
Where you end up basically--

00:57:59.130 --> 00:58:00.530
I don't know his story,
but that's my observation.

00:58:00.530 --> 00:58:02.096
But you end up applying
the same principles.

00:58:02.096 --> 00:58:03.991
If you're doing family vlogging--

00:58:03.991 --> 00:58:05.657
Exactly.
And you're good at it,

00:58:05.657 --> 00:58:07.660
you're making a reality show,

00:58:07.660 --> 00:58:10.830
and everybody knows that
reality shows are fake.

00:58:10.830 --> 00:58:12.710
So the situation and I'm not saying that,

00:58:12.710 --> 00:58:16.370
and I'm sure that that
line gets super-confusing

00:58:16.370 --> 00:58:19.930
and super gray of like, okay,
let's set this up like this,

00:58:19.930 --> 00:58:21.890
it's kind of actually
happening, but we need to do it

00:58:21.890 --> 00:58:23.410
this way for the camera.

00:58:23.410 --> 00:58:24.840
That kind of stuff happens.

00:58:24.840 --> 00:58:25.673
But--

00:58:25.673 --> 00:58:27.010
It can eat away at your soul.

00:58:27.010 --> 00:58:29.430
But the prank thing is just seedy.

00:58:29.430 --> 00:58:32.080
I mean, I love Ed Bassmaster,

00:58:32.080 --> 00:58:33.160
I've always been a fan of his.

00:58:33.160 --> 00:58:34.740
He's still around.

00:58:34.740 --> 00:58:38.470
But his pranks were always real.

00:58:38.470 --> 00:58:40.220
We used him in a video as well.

00:58:40.220 --> 00:58:42.700
And I consider him a friend,

00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:45.180
like if I saw him now,
I would just be elated

00:58:45.180 --> 00:58:46.013
to give the guy a hug.

00:58:46.013 --> 00:58:49.580
In the way that I enjoy
Ed's videos at this point

00:58:49.580 --> 00:58:51.600
is through Instagram.

00:58:51.600 --> 00:58:53.720
I follow him on Instagram
and his videos come up

00:58:53.720 --> 00:58:56.820
and it's like snippets from what he does

00:58:56.820 --> 00:58:57.653
on YouTube.

00:58:57.653 --> 00:58:59.787
And you know, he's still doing it,

00:58:59.787 --> 00:59:00.980
